\p{Reading. The three switches together take 3.8\% (Init), 4.4\% (Std), 1.5\% (Cedar slice), 0.2\% (reachability) of the instructions and are neutral on memory. Each alone is 1.4-1.8\% on the libraries and below 1\% on the Cedar slice. In CPU seconds the Std rows show the same direction (13.1 s against 13.9 - 14.6 s), the others are inside the scatter of a loaded host; the one row pair that looks worse, reachability + m5a (two runs 0.4 s above the base at the same instruction count and the same ticks), can only be the host: inference is 1\% of that corpus. The warm in-process A/B on the JVM (\code{\verb~|work/m5/ab.sh~}: \code{\verb~|M5Bench~} alternates the two configurations in ONE process, thread CPU of the check phase; Init, eight rounds, host load 140-170): base 8.99 / 9.11 / 7.83 / 9.09 s, with m5a,pchk,m5b 8.50 / 8.66 / 8.61 / 7.81 s: -4\% in the mean, also inside the scatter.}

\p{Why so little, when MATCH answers 2.2 M of 3.2 M domains and EVAL call events fall by 18\%: the domains it answers were cheap (a flat application under the gate is one NEU probe, a tabled one is a memo hit), and the conversions that make 59\% of the records are untouched.}

\p{The two numbers the brief asked for, on Init, in-process and exact (one code state: the sandbox of 14:30Z, before the eager-reduction rule):}

\table{
\tr{\th{}\th{v0}\th{\code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~}}\th{+ m5a,pchk,m5b}\th{+ facts,m5a,pchk,m5b and the front cache}}
\tr{\td{records per unit}\td{853.3}\td{442.8}\td{423.6}\td{417.6}}
\tr{\td{run words per unit}\td{3,867.6}\td{2,290.4}\td{2,247.4}\td{2,218.3}}
\tr{\td{INFER + VTYPE call events}\td{7.33 M}\td{5.07 M}\td{not taken}\td{3.91 M}}
\tr{\td{EVAL call events}\td{13.62 M}\td{11.29 M}\td{not taken}\td{8.73 M}}
\tr{\td{ticks}\td{77.83 M}\td{56.03 M}\td{52.36 M}\td{49.62 M}}
}

\p{"Records down by a third" and "INFER + VTYPE down by a third" hold against v0 (-51\% and -47\% with every step-1 switch, facts and this wave's switches) and do NOT hold against step 1 (-5.7\% and -23\%; without \code{\verb~|facts~} -4.3\% of the records): what inference itself can still remove is bounded by the 41\% of the records it makes, and the VTYPE calls that remain after \code{\verb~|facts~} are conversions asking for the type of a neutral term.}
}

