\tr{\td{reachability}\td{+ new}\td{8.33 / 8.61}\td{8.44 / 9.08}\td{1144}\td{59.0}\td{\strong{-0.2\%}}\td{35.31 M}}
\tr{\td{reachability}\td{+ new + ic}\td{8.09 / 8.24}\td{8.15 / 8.37}\td{1145}\td{59.0}\td{-0.2\%}\td{35.31 M}}
\tr{\td{reachability}\td{+ facts + new + ic}\td{8.02 / 8.23}\td{8.19 / 8.42}\td{1145}\td{59.0}\td{-0.2\%}\td{35.27 M}}
}

\p{Reading.}

\ul{
\li{\strong{m5a,pchk,m5b: kept.} Instructions -3.7\% (Init), -4.3\% (Std), -1.5\% (Cedar slice), -0.2\% (reachability) on the newer base as on the older one; CPU -4.2\% on Init and -3.3\% on Std with both rounds below both base rounds (batch 1: Std -8\%, Init level); Cedar slice and reachability move by less than the scatter in either direction (the reachability rows of "+ new" are above the base in this batch and equal to it in batch 1, and "+ new + ic", the same work, is level here). Memory: +2 to +3 MiB. A confirmation on a quiet host is still owed for the two small corpora.}
\li{\strong{The front cache: rejected (stays off, behind its property).} It answers nearly every tabling hit (4.13 M of 4.14 M on Init), but since M1's PRUNE hashes only the kept slots the probe it replaces is cheap: -0.3\% to -0.5\% of the instructions on the libraries, +0.3\% on the Cedar slice, and no CPU gain in any pair of rows (on Std "+ new + ic" is 0.6-0.8 s ABOVE "+ new" in both rounds). Not worth a table in every session.}
\li{\strong{facts (after M4's fix of S-F1 / S-F2: static PROOF only): neutral.} -0.1\% of the instructions on Init and Std, -0.3\% on the Cedar slice, CPU inside the scatter; the derivation (0.23\% of the ticks) is paid for by the PIRR / VTYPE calls it removes and no more. The derivation cost stays far below the 2\% bound.}
\li{Not this package's, but visible in both batches: on the Cedar slice and on reachability v0 needs FEWER instructions than \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~} since M1's PRUNE (39.0 against 39.6 G; 57.4 against 59.1 G).}
\li{With the eager-reduction rule armed (after these batches) the machine declines the declarations that compare under \code{\verb~|eagerReduce~}: 155 on Init (1.1\% of its ticks) but 11 on the Cedar slice that were 18\% of the machine's ticks there (18.09 M -> 14.79 M in the final gate): what that costs through the reference engine is not in these tables.}
}
}

